 Sure! Here's a PHP function called `smart_sort_array` that meets your requirements:

```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order = 'ASC') {
    $n = count($set);
    for ($i = 0; $i < $n - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 0; $j < $n - $i - 1; $j++) {
            if (($order == 'ASC' && $set[$j]['age'] > $set[$j+1]['age']) || ($order == 'DESC' && $set[$j]['age'] < $set[$j+1]['age'])) {
                // Swap elements
                $temp = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $set[$j+1];
                $set[$j+1] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }
    return $set;
}
```

This function accepts an associative array `$set` as its first argument and an optional second argument `$order` which defaults to 'ASC' for ascending order. It uses a nested loop to compare adjacent elements in the array based on their age values and swaps them if they are in the wrong order according to the given sorting direction. Finally, it returns the sorted array.

